<title>UK: Robert Wiseman H1 profits turn higher.</title>
<headline>Robert Wiseman H1 profits turn higher.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 28</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		5.47		   vs 3.79</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.15		   vs 1.00</p>
<p> Pretax		     6.11		   vs 3.92</p>
<p> Turnover		   91.01		  vs 58.87</p>
<p> Operating profit	 6.35		   vs 3.88</p>
<p> Tax			  2.02		   vs 1.29</p>
<p> Retained profit	  3.24		   vs 1.88</p>
<p> Pay date		   Feb 20, 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  Dec 10</p>
<p>NOTE - Robert Wiseman Dairies Plc said it had experienced increased margin pressure in the second half year as a result of weak bulk cream prices and the competitive multiple retailer sector. However, the company added that it has continued to increase sales to key supermarket customers.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
